
==============================================================================
S0. Definitions, universe, inheritance
==============================================================================
f_c(x) = x^2 + c over Q.  G_n(c) = f_c^n(0) (Gleason polynomials).  N_n = numerator of f_c^n(0).
'primitive prime divisor at n' = prime p | N_n with p not dividing N_m for any m<n.
Bang/Zsigmondy universe: 2^n-1, 1<=n<=40 (exact factorization via sympy).
Critical-orbit census universe: c=a/b, b in {1,2,4,8,16,32,64}, |a|<=200, gcd(a,b)=1, 1<=n<=8;
  the integer sub-universe c in [-60,60] is contained in b=1.
Inherited and NOT re-derived: three-row typing, ord_9(2)=6 row exponents, R(n)=4n+1 fibre,
  PrePer(x^2-29/16,Q) (THM-4139 sec.1 / THM-4146 sec.1), sigma-parametrization (THM-4146 (10)),
  Psi_6 of squaring = Phi_9 Phi_21 Phi_63 (THM-4139 (37)),
  arithmetic_braids_20260917_geometry.md: eta-parabola c=-(eta^2+7)/4 and disc (eta^2+eta+7)^2 (4), the parabolic
  cycle P(x)=x^3+x^2/2-9x/4-1/8 with Phi_3=P^2 and multiplier 1 at -7/4 (9), the n=3 test f^3(0)=aQ(a,b)/b^4 with
  Q=+-1 <=> no new prime (11) and its census b<=2000, Krieger's Theorem 6.1 boundary, x=2A/C -> x^2-2 (16).
  Everything below is re-verified only where a check is printed; inherited statements are cited, not claimed.

